completion.summary:
The restore store-equality test and the rewritten restore runbook landed as ad70ec6 on origin/master.

- The test checks, in order, that:
  - the source is quiescent (its -wal holds no frames);
  - the restored engram.db's SHA-256 equals the manifest's, checked before doctor;
  - doctor reports it healthy;
  - its parsed export, minus only exported_at, equals the pre-push export and differs from the changed source.
- The runbook in off-host-backup.md retires the origin first and uses the shipped list, fetch and restore words. It says plainly that:
  - claims stay held until their recorded expiry and are then recovered with --recover;
  - issued grants expire at their recorded time, or sooner when their session's control connection is opened;
  - a begun turn has no clock end and stays open until a caller acting as its session checkpoints it;
  - restore never renews, resets or revives authority from the local clock;
  - the asserted session id is the only boundary.
- Review: round 1 and round 2 each had a Medium on the authority boundary wording, both fixed. Round 3 on freeze 64d2877b was clean (Codex session-9902, Claude session-9903).
- Gate test-92a412ea passed.
- Independent evaluation passed both criteria.
- Follow-up: the begun-turn gap is filed as w-d5245036da8d.
